WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.950
- What is that?

00:00:02.263 --> 00:00:04.290
- Well, I have an
announcement to make everyone.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.123
- Is that real?

00:00:05.123 --> 00:00:08.170
- Signed scripts of Timeless
the Christmas Movie,

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:10.972
Part One and Part Two,
just for you from the cast.

00:00:10.972 --> 00:00:14.159
(audience cheering)

00:00:14.159 --> 00:00:16.030
- Oh my gosh,

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.270
you are so kind

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:19.120
and I kind of just hugged
your armpit, I'm sorry.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.150
- Yeah no, it's okay.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:22.210
- I didn't wanna lose them.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:23.850
Oh my gosh, thank you.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:24.840
- Oh my god thank you,

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.133
you single-handedly saved
our show twice I think.

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:28.030
- I did not,

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:30.490
but I do love that they
listened a little bit

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:31.390
because here's the thing,

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:33.340
it is such a great show,

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:34.173
I mean do you feel like

00:00:34.173 --> 00:00:35.423
you could teach history at this point?

00:00:35.423 --> 00:00:38.090
- Yes, so everyone gather around.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:40.270
Not at all, I actually just
have a really good memory

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:42.310
and I was kind of "Beautiful
Mind"-ing all of those

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:44.390
historical tales from the show,

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.980
but I get stopped all
the time when I travel

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.337
from history professors
and teachers, like,

00:00:49.337 --> 00:00:52.230
"Oh my gosh, I share
Timeless with my students",

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.437
and they'd think that I
know things and I'm like,

00:00:54.437 --> 00:00:56.657
"You don't wanna ask me about that,

00:00:56.657 --> 00:00:59.178
"but I could give you a
monologue about the cast".

00:00:59.178 --> 00:01:00.090
(laughing)

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.010
- No, but I will say

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:02.730
that's one of the reasons
why I really love the show,

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.090
I thought it was so cool how it tied in

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:05.080
to historical events,

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.490
and how it just was kind of
a really innovative show,

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:08.730
nothing had been done like that.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:11.720
- Thanks, it was like making
a different movie every week,

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.757
and you have a 12-year-old, right?

00:01:13.757 --> 00:01:15.275
- Well he's 13 now, yes.

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:17.477
- My son is 11, and it was great to just

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:19.790
a show that I could do
that he could watch.

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:20.623
- Absolutely.

